commit 4a5081a3d9a993fa77553c62196cc0a2b48ed810
Author: Steven Meng <milosteven000@gmail.com>
Date:   Wed Sep 30 20:00:41 2026 +0800

    fix: stop autolink literals at CJK punctuation (#971) (#972)
    
    A GFM autolink literal that is immediately followed by CJK prose swallowed
    that prose into its href, because the scanner only stops at whitespace and
    its trailing-punctuation trim only knows ASCII punctuation. Chinese and
    Japanese text does not use spaces, so `开 http://localhost:4321，或直接开
    library/x.png。` produced a link whose href was `http://localhost:4321，或直接开`
    and clicking it went nowhere.
    
    Split the literal at its first CJK punctuation mark instead, turning the
    trailing prose back into a text node. Ideographs are deliberately not
    boundaries, so a genuine CJK path such as /wiki/中文条目 keeps working, and
    an explicit [text](url) link is left alone (its raw source is not its text).

